    "posts": [
      {
        "number": 1,
        "text": "Compare cities against your workweek before comparing their overall scores. A recruiter taking private calls and an engineer working mostly asynchronously need different setups. Write down the conditions your work actually requires.",
        "alt": "Start with the workweek. Private calls. Focus time. Team overlap. Daily routine.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/N01-01.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 2,
        "text": "Make two lists: requirements and preferences. Example requirements might be a private call space and workable team overlap. Walkability or warm weather may be preferences. A high overall score should not hide a missing requirement.",
        "alt": "Separate requirements from preferences. Required conditions. Preferred conditions. Missing requirement.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/N01-02.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 3,
        "text": "Use the city directory to compare living-cost estimates, internet, safety, walkability and weather. Change the ranking category to match your question. Sorting by internet answers a different question from sorting by living costs.\n\nhashtagweb3.com/nomads/th",
        "alt": "Change the comparison question. Living costs. Internet. Safety. Walkability. Weather.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/N01-03.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 4,
        "text": "Treat city-level information as a starting point for checking the actual place. Ask a host about the desk, call privacy and internet at the accommodation. A city's average cannot tell you whether a particular room suits your work.",
        "alt": "Check the actual room. Desk. Call privacy. Connection. Host confirmation.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/N01-04.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 5,
        "text": "Compare the months you would be there, not only an annual weather summary. Also map team meetings to your local hours for those dates. A city can fit your preferences while the working schedule still does not fit your day.",
        "alt": "Use the dates you would stay. Monthly weather. Meeting dates. Local working hours. Daily routine.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/N01-05.jpg"
      },
      {
        "number": 6,
        "text": "End with a shortlist and an unanswered-questions column. For each city, note what needs a host quote, an employer answer or an official entry check. A useful comparison shows what you still need to verify before booking.",
        "alt": "Keep the unknowns beside the shortlist. City. Host question. Employer question. Entry check.",
        "image": "social-assets/knowledge-threads-month/images/N01-06.jpg"
      }
    ],
